# HSM collector conformance v1 — the collector session as the transport (epic #1660 step 3, ADR-0017).
# Format: case|action|arg1|arg2|...
#
# The driver owns a SCRIPTED SESSION SERVER: the server side of GET /api/sensors/session, over a
# real WebSocket. It accepts or refuses the upgrade, says hello, acknowledges request frames with
# a chosen status or not at all, and records every frame and every plain HTTP request. The
# collector under test is created with its transport set to the session and pointed at it.
#
# New verbs — the collector:
#   create_collector_on_session|max_values_in_package|collect_period_ms|request_timeout_ms
#     a collector whose transport is the collector session to the scripted server (identity and
#     access key as create_collector). request_timeout_ms is also how long a request waits for its ack.
#     A driver may shorten the pause between attempts to open a session; nothing here depends on it.
# New verbs — the script (they apply from the moment they run):
#   session_server_hello|max_frame_bytes|heartbeat_seconds   what the hello of later sessions states
#                                                            (default 4194304 and 30)
#   session_server_refuse_upgrades|status                    every upgrade is refused with this HTTP status
#   session_server_accept_upgrades                           upgrades are accepted again (the default)
#   session_server_ack|op|status                             requests of op (list, commands) are acknowledged
#                                                            with this status (default 200)
#   session_server_stay_silent|count                         the next count requests are recorded and get no ack
#   session_server_stop_answering_pings                      heartbeats are recorded and not answered
#   session_server_drop_sessions                             every open session is cut without a close handshake
# New verbs — assertions (timeout_s: polled until it holds; 0 checks once):
#   expect_session_count|count|timeout_s                     upgrades accepted so far equal count
#   expect_session_count_at_least|count|timeout_s
#   expect_refused_upgrades_at_least|count|timeout_s
#   expect_session_ints_once|start|count|timeout_s           every int value in [start, start+count) is in an
#                                                            accepted (2xx) list frame exactly once
#   expect_session_accepted_contains|op|substring|timeout_s  some accepted request of op contains the text
#   expect_session_requests_containing|op|substring|count|timeout_s
#                                                            the requests of op (acknowledged or not) whose
#                                                            frame contains the text number exactly count
#   expect_session_requests_containing_at_least|op|substring|count|timeout_s
#   expect_session_no_request_contains|substring             no request frame of any op contains the text
#   expect_session_frames_fit|max_bytes                      every request frame is at most max_bytes (UTF-8)
#   expect_no_http_requests                                  the server received nothing but upgrades
#   expect_session_upgrade_header|name|value                 a request header of the last accepted upgrade
#   expect_session_closed_normally                           the collector ended its last session with close 1000
#
# Contract notes:
# - Frames carry the WIRE format (aicontext/features/api/wire-contract/feature.md), the same bytes
#   in both collectors, so text assertions are on the wire: "Value":42, "Type":6, a path's tail.
# - "Delivered" means: in a request the scripted server acknowledged with a 2xx status.
# - A collector on a session never makes an HTTP request, in any case below.
# - Start does not wait for the session. A case that needs it up first waits for an accepted
#   registration, never for a time.
# - One kind of sensor per case: the drivers do not agree on what a sensor index counts across
#   kinds (per kind in the managed driver, creation order in the native one).

# Values and registrations travel as frames; nothing goes over HTTP; a stop closes the session.
session_carries_values_and_registrations|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
session_carries_values_and_registrations|create_int_sensor|contract/session/int
session_carries_values_and_registrations|start
session_carries_values_and_registrations|add_int|0|42|Ok|first
session_carries_values_and_registrations|expect_session_ints_once|42|1|15
session_carries_values_and_registrations|expect_session_accepted_contains|commands|contract/session/int"|15
session_carries_values_and_registrations|expect_session_accepted_contains|list|"Value":42|15
session_carries_values_and_registrations|stop
session_carries_values_and_registrations|expect_session_count|1|5
session_carries_values_and_registrations|expect_session_upgrade_header|Key|conformance-key
session_carries_values_and_registrations|expect_session_closed_normally
session_carries_values_and_registrations|expect_no_http_requests

# No session, no delivery, and no other way in: values wait in the queue while the upgrade is
# refused and arrive when it is accepted.
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|session_server_refuse_upgrades|503
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|create_int_sensor|contract/session/queued
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|start
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|add_int_sequence|1|5|100|Ok|queued
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|expect_refused_upgrades_at_least|2|20
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|expect_session_requests_containing|list|"Value"|0|0
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|expect_no_http_requests
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|session_server_accept_upgrades
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|expect_session_ints_once|100|5|20
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|stop
values_wait_while_the_upgrade_is_refused|expect_no_http_requests

# A batch that does not fit one frame is split; every frame fits the limit the hello stated.
# The 40 values queue up while the upgrade is refused, so they leave as one batch.
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|session_server_hello|2048|30
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|session_server_refuse_upgrades|503
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|create_int_sensor|contract/session/split
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|start
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|add_int_sequence|1|40|0|Ok|split
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|expect_refused_upgrades_at_least|1|20
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|session_server_accept_upgrades
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|expect_session_ints_once|0|40|20
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|expect_session_requests_containing_at_least|list|"Value"|2|0
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|expect_session_frames_fit|2048
batch_is_split_to_the_frame_limit|stop

# A value that cannot fit a frame on its own is not sent (it would close the session and come
# back for ever); the values around it are delivered.
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|session_server_hello|2048|30
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|create_string_sensor|contract/session/huge
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|start
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|add_string|0|before|Ok|small
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|add_string|0|repeat:x:5000|Ok|huge
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|add_string|0|after|Ok|small
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|expect_session_accepted_contains|list|"Value":"before"|20
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|expect_session_accepted_contains|list|"Value":"after"|20
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|expect_session_no_request_contains|xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|expect_session_frames_fit|2048
value_larger_than_a_frame_is_dropped|stop

# A request without an ack is a failed send: the session is closed (a late ack is then impossible)
# and the batch is delivered on the next session.
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|create_collector_on_session|50|20|1000
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|create_int_sensor|contract/session/no-ack
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|start
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|expect_session_accepted_contains|commands|contract/session/no-ack"|15
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|session_server_stay_silent|1
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|add_int|0|7|Ok|no-ack
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|expect_session_ints_once|7|1|25
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|expect_session_count_at_least|2|5
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|expect_session_requests_containing_at_least|list|"Value":7|2|0
request_without_an_ack_is_resent_on_a_new_session|stop

# A session that drops is opened again, and what queued up meanwhile is delivered.
dropped_session_is_reopened|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
dropped_session_is_reopened|create_int_sensor|contract/session/dropped
dropped_session_is_reopened|start
dropped_session_is_reopened|add_int|0|1|Ok|first
dropped_session_is_reopened|expect_session_ints_once|1|1|15
dropped_session_is_reopened|session_server_refuse_upgrades|503
dropped_session_is_reopened|session_server_drop_sessions
dropped_session_is_reopened|add_int|0|2|Ok|outage
dropped_session_is_reopened|add_int|0|3|Ok|outage
dropped_session_is_reopened|expect_refused_upgrades_at_least|1|20
dropped_session_is_reopened|session_server_accept_upgrades
dropped_session_is_reopened|expect_session_ints_once|1|3|25
dropped_session_is_reopened|expect_session_count_at_least|2|5
dropped_session_is_reopened|stop
dropped_session_is_reopened|expect_no_http_requests

# Heartbeat: a server that sends nothing for two and a half heartbeats is given up, and the
# session is opened again. heartbeat_seconds is 1, so the silence is 2.5 s of wall clock.
silent_server_is_given_up_and_the_session_reopened|session_server_hello|4194304|1
silent_server_is_given_up_and_the_session_reopened|session_server_stop_answering_pings
silent_server_is_given_up_and_the_session_reopened|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
silent_server_is_given_up_and_the_session_reopened|start
silent_server_is_given_up_and_the_session_reopened|expect_session_count_at_least|2|25
silent_server_is_given_up_and_the_session_reopened|stop

# The status of an ack is the HTTP status the request would have got, and means the same.
# A registration answered 4xx is final: it is not sent again (#1659 A2). The later registration
# is the clock: a registration that went back to the queue would have been sent again by then.
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|create_int_sensor|contract/session/first
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|start
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|expect_session_accepted_contains|commands|contract/session/first"|15
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|session_server_ack|commands|400
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|create_int_sensor|contract/session/rejected
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|expect_session_requests_containing|commands|contract/session/rejected"|1|15
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|session_server_ack|commands|200
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|create_int_sensor|contract/session/later
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|expect_session_accepted_contains|commands|contract/session/later"|15
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|expect_session_requests_containing|commands|contract/session/rejected"|1|0
registration_refused_with_4xx_is_final|stop

# A value batch answered 4xx goes back to the queue and is sent again, as over HTTP.
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|create_int_sensor|contract/session/again
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|start
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|expect_session_accepted_contains|commands|contract/session/again"|15
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|session_server_ack|list|400
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|add_int|0|9|Ok|refused
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|expect_session_requests_containing_at_least|list|"Value":9|2|20
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|session_server_ack|list|200
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|expect_session_ints_once|9|1|20
value_batch_refused_with_4xx_is_sent_again|stop

# The session has no op for a file value yet. It is refused where it is sent: it never becomes a
# frame and it is not sent over HTTP either. Checked after the stop, whose drain would have sent
# anything that was queued (the session is up: the registration was acknowledged on it).
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|create_collector_on_session|50|20|5000
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|create_file_sensor|contract/session/file|report|txt
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|start
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|expect_session_accepted_contains|commands|contract/session/file"|15
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|add_file_value|0|content|Ok|file
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|stop
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|expect_session_requests_containing|list|"body"|0|0
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|expect_session_no_request_contains|"Type":6
file_value_is_not_sent_on_a_session|expect_no_http_requests
